# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# EVERY value here is optional. The app builds, launches and works with all of them
# unset — that is the state of a fresh clone, and it is tested that way.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JS bundle at build time by Metro, so anything here is
# extractable from the APK. Only public keys belong in this file. A real secret
# (the Sentry auth token, the Supabase service role key) goes in EAS Secrets and NEVER
# in any .env that could be committed by accident.

# Sentry. A DSN is a public ingestion key, not a credential: it lets a client SEND events
# and grants no read access to your data. Safe in the bundle; protected by Sentry's own
# rate limits and inbound filters. Unset = crash reporting is off and every Sentry call
# in the app is a no-op.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# The force-update kill switch payload. See DECISIONS.md, 2026-09-10.
# Unset = the check is skipped and launch proceeds.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FORCE_UPDATE_URL=

# Supabase, from Slice 8. The anon key is public and protected by Row Level Security.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
